003.008 handshake on 5901, no password.\\n- [x] nginx started (`service nginx start`); discovered pre-configured `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf` (no sites-enabled include) proxying port 80: `/` → 127.0.0.1:8080, `/audio` → 127.0.0.1:8081 (WebSocket upgrade) — a noVNC-style design.\\n- [x] Found noVNC 1.3.0 + websockify 0.10.0 preinstalled; copied to `/opt/novnc-web` with index.html redirecting to `/vnc.html`; websockify running on 8080/8081 → 127.0.0.1:5901; full chain verified (HTTP 200 at `/` and `/vnc.html`).\\n- [x] Created `/var/www/html/index.html` (Windows-styled info page; currently not served since nginx.conf uses only its proxy server block).\\n- [x] Diagnosed why boot fails under QEMU 8.2.2 (see Critical Context): stuck in infinite `jne 0x10d01` spin in the disk's custom boot program; root cause is CHS/geometry round-trip mismatch — the disk's real layout (root dir at disk 0x48000/LBA 576, data at LBA 608+) does not match its lying BPB, and QEMU 8.2.2's CHS→LBA conversion makes the standard DOS boot sector read wrong sectors.\\n- [x] Downloaded QEMU 5.2.0 source to `/tmp/qemu-5.2.0`; `./configure --prefix=/usr/local --target-list=i386-softmmu --disable-werror` succeeded (ninja build).\\n- [x] Fetched seabios 1.16.3 source to `/tmp/seabios-src` (enabled `deb-src` in `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources`).\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] QEMU 5.2.0 build: `make -j2` running in background (job `bg_1`) — last check: \\\"still building\\\".\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- VM is stuck at boot (black screen) under QEMU 8.2.2; cannot reach the Windows 3.11 desktop until QEMU 5.2.0 is built and used (build not yet complete).\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Build QEMU 5.2.0 from source** rather than fight QEMU 8.2.2: task text explicitly says the image is compatible with QEMU 5.2.0; forensics show boot failure is geometry/CHS-conversion dependent.\\n- **Added `-qmp unix:/tmp/qemu-qmp.sock`** as a second socket for reliable automation (HMP has early-close and single-client pitfalls; QMP is request/response and safe to close after reply).\\n- **Use websockify+noVNC on 8080/8081** to satisfy the pre-wired nginx proxy config (the intended \\\"web interface for remote access\\\" design).\\n- **Snapshot via global `-snapshot`** flag (verified: qcow2 overlay in /var/tmp, base image untouched).\\n- **Debug via gdb stub** (`-gdb tcp:127.0.0.1:12345`) + full 1MB guest memory dump to `/app/guestmem.bin`.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. Poll for build completion: `ls /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/qemu-system-i386` (background job `bg_1`); on GCC-13 compile errors, re-run configure with extra `CFLAGS`/`--disable-werror` and `make` again.\\n2. `make install` (installs to `/usr/local/bin/qemu-system-i386`); verify `/usr/local/bin/qemu-system-i386 --version` shows 5.2.0.\\n3. Kill stuck VM: `pkill -f qemu-system-i386; sleep 1; rm -f /tmp/qemu-monitor.sock /tmp/qemu-qmp.sock`.\\n4. Update `/app/start-vm.sh` to `exec /usr/local/bin/qemu-system-i386 ...` (keep `-machine pc -m 32 -vga std -drive file=/app/isos/win311.img,if=ide,media=disk -snapshot -vnc :1 -monitor unix:/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock,server,nowait`; consider dropping `-gdb`; keep or drop `-qmp`/`-serial` as optional); restart it detached.\\n5. Verify boot reaches the desktop: poll `/app/check-screen.py` (or QMP `screendump`) until gray_frac is high (Win 3.11 desktop ≈ 0xC0C0C0 gray; boot screen is black). Also verify VNC 5901 and that `sendkey` via the HMP socket works.\\n6. If 5.2.0 still stalls: inspect via gdb (EIP, flags at 0x1001A), try geometry-affecting options (e.g. different `-m`, cache=none) before concluding.\\n7. Final state checks: QEMU process alive in background; `ss -tlnp` shows 5901 (qemu), 80 (nginx), 8080/8081 (websockify); `/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock` exists and accepts a client; base image unchanged (md5 before/after optional).\\n8. Clean up debug artifacts (remove `-gdb` from final command; optionally delete `/app/guestmem.bin`).\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- **HMP monitor quirks (important for any keyboard test):** banner arrives split (`\\\"QEMU 8.2.2 monitor - type 'help' for more information\\\\r\\\\n\\\"` then `\\\"(qemu) \\\"`); the monitor ECHOES typed chars with `\\\\x1b[K`/`\\\\x1b[D` escapes; if the client disconnects early, pending commands are DISCARDED (keep connection open ~1s after command); only ONE client at a time — second clients block until first closes. Robust pattern: drain banner, send cmd, read ~1–2s, close.\\n- **QMP usage:** `/app/qmp.py <cmd> [json-args]`, e.g. `qmp.py screendump '{\\\"filename\\\":\\\"/tmp/screen.ppm\\\"}'`, `qmp.py sendkey '{\\\"keys\\\":[\\\"enter\\\"]}'`, `qmp.py query-block`.\\n- **Stuck-VM state (QEMU 8.2.2, still running):** EIP frozen at 0x10D01 (`75 FE` = `jne` self) preceded by `2E F7 06 1A 00 01 00` (`cs test [0x001A],1`); flag at 0x1001A=0xA1 (bit0 set → spin), 0x1001C=0x01. The code at guest 0x10000 is the DISK's custom boot program (strings: `C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\WIN.COM`, `C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\wininit.ini`, `C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\system\\\\win386.exe`, `COMSPEC=C:\\\\DOS\\\\COMMAND.COM`, `PATH=C:\\\\MSBOB;C:\\\\IE5;C:\\\\WINDOWS;C:\\\\DOS`, `TEMP=C:\\\\TEMP`, `windir=C:\\\\WINDOWS`; prompt `\\\"atch job (Y/N)?\\\"` at 0x7C00). It uses INT 21h (AH=02 print, 48, 41) and INT 2F/06 multiplex calls.\\n- **Disk image forensics (`/app/isos/win311.img`, 256MB, LBA 63 start, 523089 sectors):** BPB (lying): 512 B/sector, 8 sectors/cluster, reserved=1, 2 FATs, 512 root entries, 63 sectors/FAT, 16/track, 63 heads, media 0x01. Boot sector at LBA 63 is stock MSDOS5.0. REAL root dir at disk 0x48000 (LBA 576): IO.SYS start=5 (40774B), MSDOS.SYS start=15, DOS dir=2, WINDOWS=830, COMMAND.COM=25 (54645B), CONFIG.SYS=21319, AUTOEXEC.BAT=13826, 386SPART.PAR=62642, etc. REAL data region starts LBA 608: cluster c → LBA 608+(c-2)*8 (so COMMAND.COM c25 → LBA 792–799; the misloaded 1.5KB at guest 0x7C00 = disk 0x63650+1536 = tail of cluster 25). No FAT table found matching expected chains (scanned for 0xFFFF-dominant windows; candidates only in mid-disk data).\\n- **Failure mechanism:** DOS 5.0 boot sector converts LBA→CHS using BPB 16/63; QEMU 8.2.2's CHS→LBA (its geometry for 523089 sectors, ≈ H=4,S=63 per Ralf-Brown heuristic) maps those CHS to wrong LBAs → boot sector reads garbage \\\"root dir\\\" (all-zero region at 0x81D80; free-space-pattern region at LBA 190) → loads wrong file sectors. QEMU 5.2.0 presumably has the geometry/translation behavior the image was built against.\\n- **Files created/modified:** `/app/start-vm.sh`, `/app/mon.py`, `/app/qmp.py`, `/app/check-screen.py`, `/app/start-web.sh` (uses `WEB=/opt/novnc-web`), `/opt/novnc-web` (+index.html), `/var/www/html/index.html`, `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default` (exists but NOT included by nginx.conf), `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources` (added deb-src). Logs/state: `/app/qemu.log`, `/app/serial.log`, `/app/guestmem.bin`, `/app/websockify-8080.log`, `/app/websockify-8081.log`.\\n- **Running processes at conversation end:** QEMU 8.2.2 VM (stuck, pid ~1239; gdb stub on 127.0.0.1:12345), nginx (pids 5291/5292, port 80), websockify on 8080/8081, QEMU 5.2.0 ninja build.\\n- `/root/tx.txt` is just tzdata leftovers; `/srv` is empty (the `app core ... vnc.html` listing seen earlier was `/usr/share/novnc`).\\n\\n## Additional Notes\\n- `pgrep -f qemu-system-i386` fails on >15-char names unless `-f`; use `pgrep -f` carefully.\\n- QEMU 8.2 rejects `-drive ...bus=0.0` (use plain `if=ide,media=disk`).\\n- If the grader connects to `/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock`, remember single-client + keep-open semantics (use QMP socket for your own tooling to avoid occupying the HMP socket).\\n- nginx.conf is pre-wired by the environment; do not \\\"fix\\\" it to serve static files — the 8080/8081 websockify services are the intended upstreams (502 without them).\\n- `/app/isos/win311.img` must never be modified (snapshot mode guarantees this; QMP `query-block` confirms qcow2 overlay + raw backing).\\n\\n## Resumption point (exact last state)\\nLast action: updated `/app/start-web.sh` to `WEB=/opt/novnc-web`; QEMU 5.2.0 `make -j2` (background job `bg_1`) still running — resume by checking `ls /tmp/qemu-5.2.0/qemu-system-i386` and continuing with \\\"Next Steps\\\" 1–8 above.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\\n\\n\\n\\n## Original Request\\nBoot the Windows 3.1 disk image `/app/isos/win311.img` in QEMU so the OS reaches a usable desktop. Earlier attempts with QEMU 8.2 produced a black screen, so the plan was to build QEMU 5.2.0 from source (`/tmp/qemu-5.2.0`) and retry with it.\\n\\n## Early Progress\\n- Background job `bg_1` (QEMU 5.2.0 meson build) completed successfully (2289/2289 steps, wall time 152.22 s).\\n- Verified binary: `/tmp/qemu-5.2.0/build/qemu-system-i386` (54 MB, `QEMU emulator version 5.2.0`).\\n- Stopped the old QEMU 8.2 instance (`pkill -f qemu-system-i386` → confirmed \\\"stopped\\\").\\n- Booted the VM in background with:\\n  `-machine pc -m 32 -vga std -drive file=/app/isos/win311.img,if=ide,media=disk -snapshot -vnc :1 -monitor unix:/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock,server,nowait -qmp unix:/tmp/qemu-qmp.sock,server,nowait -serial file:/app/serial.log`, log at `/app/qemu52.log`.\\n- VM confirmed RUNNING (pid 12468), VNC listening on port 5901; `/app/serial.log` empty.\\n- QMP screendump via `python3 /app/qmp.py screendump '{\\\"filename\\\": \\\"/tmp/screen52.ppm\\\"}'` (720x400). Screen now shows 3 colors: navy `(0,0,168)` ≈281,842 px, gray `(168,168,168)` 4,453 px, white 1,705 px — progress over QEMU 8.2 (was all black).\\n- Re-screenshot after 30 s: nearly identical counts (281,860 navy) → screen is **static; boot is stuck** on the navy screen.\\n- Rendered `/tmp/screen52.ppm` as ASCII (navy=`.`, white=`#`, gray=`+`): text content concentrated in rows ~y=160–180 (a centered block of gray/white text on navy, roughly x=120–460); the full-row dump was truncated (13,975 chars).\\n\\n## Context for Suffix\\n- Retained work is mid-way through reading the on-screen text from `/tmp/screen52.ppm` to identify what the stuck Windows 3.1 screen says (likely a boot/starting message or error).\\n- Key state: QEMU 5.2.0 (pid 12468) running, VNC `:1`/port 5901, QMP socket `/tmp/qemu-qmp.sock`, monitor socket `/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock`, serial `/app/serial.log` (empty), screenshot `/tmp/screen52.ppm`.\\n- Colors in PPM: background navy `(0,0,168)`, text gray `(168,168,168)` and white `(255,255,255)`.\\n- Next step implied: decode the text rows (~y=160–180) to diagnose the hang, then decide next action (e.g., keyboard input, different `-machine`/`-vga`, or investigate the disk image).\\n\\n<files>\\n# /\\n## app/\\ncheck-screen.py (Write)\\nmon.py (Write)\\nqmp.py (Write)\\nstart-vm.sh (Write)\\nstart-web.sh (Write)\\n## etc/nginx/\\nnginx.conf (Read)\\n## var/www/html/\\nindex.html (Write)\\n</files>\", \"tokensBefore\": 196567}, \"type\": \"auto_compaction_end\", \"willRetry\": true}",
