      "thought": "These are the font tables (VGA fonts in LBA 96–157!). The custom boot program contains an embedded font (the \"!\"-separated thing is the font for characters with the 0x21 prefix… actually these look like font bitmaps stored with each glyph prefixed by a character code).\n\nNote: LBA 96–157 (offset 49152–81408) contains the font. The boot program (0x7C00 = LBA 0) is only 512 bytes; the rest of the program is… where? According to forensics, the code at guest 0x10000 contains the strings C:\\WINDOWS\\WIN.COM etc. Those strings should also be in the disk image. They're not in the first 64KB — meaning the program is loaded from a later LBA.\n\nFrom the earlier full-disk string scan (the truncated output), I could see the Winbrick manual at LBA 115548 onward. The custom boot program's strings (WIN.COM, wininit.ini, \"atch job\") — let me search specifically for those in the disk.\n",
