`/etc/nginx/nginx.conf` proxies port 80: `/`→127.0.0.1:8080, `/audio`→127.0.0.1:8081 (WebSocket). noVNC 1.3.0 + websockify 0.10.0 copied to `/opt/novnc-web`; websockify on 8080/8081 → 127.0.0.1:5901; HTTP 200 at `/` and `/vnc.html`.\\n- [x] Diagnosed QEMU 8.2.2 boot failure (CHS/geometry mismatch; stuck in `jne 0x10d01` spin).\\n- [x] Built QEMU 5.2.0 from source: binary at `/tmp/qemu-5.2.0/build/qemu-system-i386` (54MB, `QEMU emulator version 5.2.0`).\\n- [x] Killed old QEMU 8.2.2; booted VM under QEMU 5.2.0 in background (pid 12468) with: `-machine pc -m 32 -vga std -drive file=/app/isos/win311.img,if=ide,media=disk -snapshot -vnc :1 -monitor unix:/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock,server,nowait -qmp unix:/tmp/qemu-qmp.sock,server,nowait -serial file:/app/serial.log`, log `/app/qemu52.log`.\\n- [x] Confirmed QEMU 5.2.0 is the correct version: screen is no longer pure black — it now shows a proper CGA-palette boot dialog.\\n- [x] Decoded on-screen layout via pixel analysis (PPM screendump, 720x400): CGA 4-color palette only — navy `(0,0,168)` bg, gray `(168,168,168)`, white `(255,255,255)`.\\n- [x] Established the boot is a **fast, deterministic fake \\\"Windows 3.1\\\" splash sequence** (not real Windows): after `system_reset`, timeline = 1.1s black+gray BIOS text → 3.1s cyan splash window → 4.1s navy dialog (stable). Boot to dialog ≈ 4s.\\n- [x] Discovered blinking cursor at `x 477-485, y 269-270` (end of body line 2) → screen is waiting for input.\\n- [x] Confirmed disk is a genuine MSDOS5.0 + Windows 3.1 + \\\"Winbrick\\\"/MSBOB/IE5 image: LBA 0 = standard MBR (FAT16 part, LBA 63, 523089 sec); LBA 63 = stock MSDOS5.0 boot sector; LBA 1-20 all zeros.\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] Identifying the correct input to advance from the navy \\\"Windows 3.1\\\" dialog to the desktop (Enter proved wrong → black screen; mouse click and other keys not yet tested).\\n- [ ] Re-capturing and correctly decoding the splash/dialog text (cyan window text lines and navy dialog title/body).\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- Pressing **Enter** (`ret`) advanced the screen to a **pure black `(0,0,0)` screen** (288000 px, unchanged for 60+ s, serial.log empty, VM status \\\"running\\\") — appears to be a crash/hang or a non-rendering mode. The navy dialog must be reached again (via `system_reset`) and a *different* input tried.\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Use QEMU 5.2.0** (built from source): task explicitly says the image is compatible with 5.2.0; 8.2.2 fails due to CHS/LBA geometry conversion.\\n- **Snapshot via `-snapshot`** (qcow2 overlay in /var/tmp; base image untouched; verified via QMP `query-block`).\\n- **websockify+noVNC on 8080/8081** to satisfy the pre-wired nginx proxy design.\\n- **QMP socket `/tmp/qemu-qmp.sock`** for reliable request/response automation; keep HMP `/tmp/qemu-monitor.sock` free (single-client, early-close discards pending commands).\\n- **Treat the on-screen \\\"dialog\\\" as the correct interactive checkpoint** (deterministic, CGA-palette) rather than a hang; find its expected input rather than changing machine/vga.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. `system_reset` the VM (QMP) and poll screendump until the navy dialog returns (~4s); confirm via color counts (navy ≈281860, gray ≈4435, white ≈1705).\\n2. Try a **mouse click** on the dialog (HMP `mouse_event left down` / `left up`, or QMP `mouse_event`) — classic \\\"Welcome to Windows 3.1\\\" expects a mouse click, not Enter. Screendump + diff to detect change.\\n3. If mouse click fails, try single keys `y`, `n`, `a` via HMP `sendkey`, and arrows; screendump + diff after each.\\n4. If still stuck, decode the dialog text fully (see Critical Context) and inspect the disk boot program (disassemble LBA 63 / find where the splash strings live) to learn the exact expected key.\\n5. Once the desktop (CGA gray/white UI) is confirmed stable, leave VM running; re-verify VNC 5901, nginx 80, websockify 8080/8081 all alive.\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- **Display/palette (QEMU 5.2.0, `-vga std`, 720x400 PPM):** CGA