ge\" search: the 0x4253ec4 context contains \"nd Warnning Message\" — that's in the LE file. Are there other hits for \"Warnning\"? Let me search.\n\nIf the string \"No RTL8029  adapter Warnning Message\" (the title) only exists in the LE file, then it's the LE file that's drawing the dialog (a Windows program drawing in CGA mode? Unlikely, but…).\n\nOr, the DOS program that's drawing the dialog has the strings XOR-encoded/obfuscated.\n\nLet me search the entire image for \"Warnning\", \"Press any key to continue\" (exact match), \"adapter exists\", and \"RTL8029\".\n\n\n\nLet me search the whole image for the unique dialog strings:\n\n",
