      "source": "agent",
      "thought": "The build tree is intact. QEMU 5.2 has the following:\n- `hw/net/ne2000.c` (shared NE2000 register emulation — `NE2000State` with NE2000_COMMON)\n- `hw/net/ne2000-pci.c` (PCI wrapper for NE2000)\n- `hw/net/ne2000-isa.c` (ISA wrapper)\n\nThe cleanest approach: copy `ne2000-pci.c` and make `rtl8029-pci.c` — a PCI device with vendor 0x10ec/device 0x8029 that wraps the same NE2000 register emulation.\n\nTo use as a template, let's take a look at ne2000-pci.c.\n\n\n\nLet me examine the ne2000-pci.c wrapper to model my RTL8029 device on it:\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8c1e1c8b0add25a1@1098:2",
